  "notes": "ねばねば is an onomatopoeic word describing sticky textures, especially in food.\n\nCOMMON EXAMPLES OF ねばねば FOODS:\n- ⟦{納豆|なっとう}→納豆：04930_nattou⟧ (natto/fermented soybeans)\n- ⟦オクラ→オクラ：10242_okura⟧ (okra)\n- ⟦{山芋|やまいも}→山芋：22494_yamaimo⟧/⟦{長芋|ながいも}→長芋：24129_nagaimo⟧ (mountain yam)\n- めかぶ (mekabu seaweed)\n\nHEALTH CONTEXT:\n- ねばねば foods are considered healthy in Japanese cuisine\n- The stickiness is thought to aid ⟦{消化|しょうか}→消化：04200_shouka⟧ and provide ⟦{栄養|えいよう}→栄養：01882_eiyou⟧\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦べたべた→べたべた：05171_betabeta⟧: sticky (unpleasant, like sweat or glue)\n- ⟦ぬるぬる→ぬるぬる：05173_nurunuru⟧: slimy (often negative)",
